  "body": "If any new elements are added to HTML (including custom elements) starting with \"rss\" or \"feed\" the sniffing algorithm will mis-detect text/html as application/rss+xml or application/atom+xml.\r\n\r\nFor example if `<feedback>` or `<feeder>` are added to the HTML spec, or if the user creates custom elements like `<rss-editor>` or `<feedback-form>`",
